    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Building a sphere with ~150 scattered intersecting cylinders and boolean-unioning everything into one solid. ScatterOnSurface distributes cylinders across the sphere UV; Boolean union fuses the scatter compound with the base sphere. WARNING: unioning 100+ intersecting solids is computationally expensive and may cause long evaluation or kernel timeouts."
    },
    {
      "role": "system",
      "content": "Engine fault (does not count against repair budget, 1/3) — retrying."
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The Boolean union of 150 intersecting cylinders + sphere causes a kernel crash (opaque code 11078112) — OpenCascade cannot fuse that many overlapping solids in one operation. Instead, drop the union entirely and keep the sphere and scattered cylinders as SEPARATE leaf nodes for multi-color rendering. The visual effect of cylinders piercing the sphere is preserved without the costly boolean. Reduced count to 80 for better performance."
    },
    {
      "role": "system",
      "content": "[Patch] 2 removedEdgeIds entries matched NO edge (already gone or never existed) — nothing was removed for: scatter->union; sphere->union. This usually means those edges were already dropped or renamed — do NOT keep retrying them. Use the edge ids shown in the graph state, {\"source\",\"target\"} objects, or \"source->target\" strings. Edges that DO exist on those nodes: sphere->scatter.surface, cylinder->scatter.shape"
    },
    {
      "role": "system",
      "content": "Engine fault (does not count against repair budget, 2/3) — retrying."
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Sphere pierced by ~50 vertical cylinders arranged in latitude rings, rendered as separate colored leaves without boolean union"
    }
